This question tests CISSP-aligned incident response and forensics skills in a serverless, multi-cloud context. It evaluates understanding of detection telemetry, containment procedures, evidence handling, chain of custody maintenance, and cross-provider playbooks.

Key Concepts

- Incident response lifecycles across AWS Lambda, Google Cloud Functions, and on-premises FaaS
- Evidence preservation and time synchronization across cloud providers
- Cross-cloud playbooks and tooling coordination

Code Example

```javascript
// Example: mock evidence hash calculation
const crypto = require('crypto');

function calculateEvidenceHash(filePath, content) {
  const hash = crypto.createHash('sha256');
  hash.update(content);
  const evidenceHash = hash.digest('hex');

  return {
    filePath,
    evidenceHash,
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
  };
}

module.exports = { calculateEvidenceHash };
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes data governance, access control, and incident response fundamentals for beginner CISSP candidates, with a realistic data-import scenario.

## Key Concepts

- Data classification and handling
- RBAC/ABAC and just-in-time access
- Data provenance and SBOM concepts
- Encryption at rest and in transit; KMS/key rotation
- Immutable audit logging and incident response/testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Validate payload schema and attach a signed attestation
function validateAndSign(payload, signer) {
  // simple schema check
  if (!payload || !payload.data) throw new Error('Invalid');
  const attestation = signer.sign(JSON.stringify(payload));
  return { payload, attestation };
}
```

